::PC_U02_L05_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L05_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.3
Question:
Which reasoning best supports verifying the identity sin²(x)+cos²(x)=1 in a solution?.
{
~A. Substitute one angle only and assume the identity is always true#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
=B. Use the Pythagorean identity and show that the left side simplifies to the right side#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~C. Move terms randomly until both sides look similar#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. Divide by sine even when sine may equal zero#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
}

